 for the empty set?","options":["$\\{0\\}$","$\\{\\varnothing\\}$","$\\varnothing$","$0$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"2250251d39a8e075010e3c77","time_limit":20},{"id":"year-1-1a-math-i-calculus-empty-set-html-q03","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which statement correctly distinguishes $\\varnothing$ from $\\{0\\}$?","options":["Both have no elements.","$\\varnothing$ has one element, while $\\{0\\}$ has none.","They are equal because $0$ means nothing.","$\\varnothing$ has no elements, while $\\{0\\}$ has one element."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b9c152a6be12642fd9de98d5","time_limit":30},{"id":"year-1-1a-math-i-calculus-empty-set-html-q04","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Which set is empty as a subset of $\\mathbb{R}$?","options":["$\\{x\\in\\mathbb{R}\\colon x=0\\}$","$\\{x\\in\\mathbb{R}\\colon x^2+1=0\\}$","$\\{x\\in\\mathbb{R}\\colon x^2=1\\}$","$\\{x\\in\\mathbb{R}\\colon x\\ge0\\}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"3d5edaf85bd48f84dd2e2bae","time_limit":20},{"id":"year-1-1a-math-i-calculus-empty-set-html-q05","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"How many elements does $\\varnothing$ contain?","options":["$0$","$1$","$2$","Infinitely many"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"fd866809cd7f3c3917b4006d","time_limit":20},{"id":"year-1-1a-math-i-calculus-empty-set-html-q06","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Which set is not empty?","options":["$\\varnothing$","$\\{\\varnothing\\}$","$\\{x\\in\\mathbb{N}\\colon x \\lt 0\\}$","$\\{x\\in\\mathbb{R}\\colon x\\ne x\\}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"fa5bd5f630e7431489a3f911","time_limit":20},{"id":"year-1-1a-math-i-calculus-empty-set-html-q07","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which relation holds between $\\varnothing$ and every set $A$?","options":["$A\\subseteq\\varnothing$","$\\varnothing\\in A$","$\\varnothing\\subseteq A$","$A=\\varnothing$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"0d26f87cb15998d2b8ee7797","time_limit":30},{"id":"year-1-1a-math-i-calculus-empty-set-html-q08","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Why is $\\varnothing\\subseteq A$ true for every set $A$?","options":["Because there is no element of $\\varnothing$ that could fail to belong to $A$","Because every set $A$ contains $\\varnothing$ as one of its elements, listed or not.","Because $A$ must have at least one element","Because $\\varnothing$ and $A$ have the same elements"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"40f0cc6da9ec951b4b3e097a","time_limit":35},{"id":"year-1-1a-math-i-calculus-empty-set-html-q09","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"How many empty sets are there?","options":["There are many different empty sets, one for each universe.","The empty set contains itself as an element by definition.","There is exactly one empty set.","The empty set is equal to every set with cardinality one."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"f8299635f16afa192d5b1539","time_limit":30},{"id":"year-1-1a-math-i-calculus-empty-set-html-q10","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"For any set $A$, which set equals $A\\cup\\varnothing$?","options":["$A$","$\\varnothing$","$\\{A\\}$","$A\\setminus\\varnothing$ only when $A$ is finite"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b028a43ed76d85c397b83d8b","time_limit":30},{"id":"year-1-1a-math-i-calculus-empty-set-html-q11","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"For any set $A$, which set equals $A\\cap\\varnothing$?","options":["$A$","$\\{\\varnothing\\}$","$\\varnothing$","$A$ only if $A$ is non-empty"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"12c5e112ce8c42799ac9de19","time_limit":30},{"id":"year-1-1a-math-i-calculus-empty-set-html-q12","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which description correctly captures the empty set?","options":["It gives a one-element set used to represent the number zero.","It gives the unique set with no elements, a subset of every set.","It gives the set of all elements not belonging to a chosen set.","It gives a set with no elements that is an element of every set."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"d920f8d30a0e5a2c301d3a28","time_limit":30},{"id":"year-1-1a-math-i-calculus-empty-set-html-q13","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which of the following is a mistake to avoid when working with the empty set $\\varnothing$?","options":["Using $\\varnothing\\subseteq A$ for an arbitrary set $A$","Treating $\\varnothing$ and $\\{0\\}$ as the same set","Saying that $\\varnothing$ has cardinality $0$","Using $\\varnothing$ to denote the set with no elements"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"d37310f264af98c2b2d3a9e9","time_limit":30},{"id":"year-1-1a-math-i-calculus-empty-set-html-q14","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Which set equals $\\{x\\in\\mathbb{R}\\colon x^2+1=0\\}$?","options":["$\\{0\\}$","$\\{-1,1\\}$","$\\{\\varnothing\\}$","$\\varnothing$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"5ff56aed5fa8832aebe239d6","time_limit":30},{"id":"year-1-1a-math-i-calculus-empty-set-html-q15","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which statement correctly distinguishes $\\varnothing\\subseteq A$ from $\\varnothing\\in A$?","options":["$\\varnothing\\subseteq A$ is always true, but $\\varnothing\\in A$ depends on $A$.","$\\varnothing\\in A$ is always true, but $\\varnothing\\subseteq A$ depends on $A$.","Both are always true for every set $A$.","Both mean exactly the same thing."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9783de6c6d00e95741277129","time_limit":40},{"id":"year-1-1a-math-i-calculus-empty-set-html-q16","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"If $B\\subseteq\\varnothing$, what must be true?","options":["$B=\\{\\varnothing\\}$","$B$ has exactly one element","$\\varnothing\\in B$","$B=\\varnothing$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"f28d3bd3605707b75e32d4a3","time_limit":40},{"id":"year-1-1a-math-i-calculus-empty-set-html-q17","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"Which relation between $\\varnothing$ and $\\{\\varnothing\\}$ is correct?","options":["$\\varnothing=\\{\\varnothing\\}$","$\\{\\varnothing\\}$ contains two elements","$\\varnothing\\not\\subseteq\\{\\varnothing\\}$","$\\varnothing\\in\\{\\varnothing\\}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b0592448e417bb286811c02d","time_limit":40},{"id":"year-1-1a-math-i-calculus-empty-set-html-q18","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Why does the statement “every element of $\\varnothing$ has property $P$” count as true?","options":["Because there is no element of $\\varnothing$ that violates $P$","Because $P$ is automatically true for every object","Because $\\varnothing$ contains a hidden element satisfying $P$","Because the statement means that $P$ is false"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"2a4dbbdad3699a29532f1cff","time_limit":40},{"id":"year-1-1a-math-i-calculus-empty-set-html-q19","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"Which equality is correct for every set $A$?","options":["$A\\setminus A=\\varnothing$","$A\\setminus\\varnothing=\\varnothing$","$\\varnothing\\setminus A=A$","$A\\cup\\varnothing=\\varnothing$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"3a4ef4b0ea0d09032002df0a","time_limit":40},{"id":"year-1-1a-math-i-calculus-empty-set-html-q20","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"Which set has cardinality $1$ rather than $0$?","options":["$\\varnothing$","$\\{\\varnothing\\}$","$\\{x\\in\\mathbb{R}\\colon x^2+1=0\\}$","$\\{x\\in\\mathbb{N}\\colon x \\lt 0\\}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"881965effeb00b9092519a08","time_limit":40}]}}